By Xpath
=============
- xpath is path of element from any html or xml document
- xpath identify elements from DOM(document object model)
- xpath travel in both direction 
- xpath support multiple methods
- xpath axies we can interact DOM

--------HTML DOM----------

<html>--------------root element/node
<head>
<head>

<body>
<a>
<div>----------------element
<input>
</body>

</html>
=======================================
XPath Types
=============
1.Absolute Xpath
=================
- It identify element form root node
- It starts with '/'

/html/body/div[2]/div/div/div/div[2]/div/form/div[1]/input

2.Relative Xpath
==================
- Relative xpath identify element from its relative property
- It starts with '//'

//*[@id="input-email"]

*: any tag

================================
Syntax
===========
//tagname[@attribute='value']

================================
xpath with indexing and position

(xpath)[index]
or
(xpath)[position()=index]

====================================================
Xpath methods
====================
1.text()
===========
- text() identify element based visible text
- text() never ignore white space
 
Syntax:
===========
//tagname[text()='text']


2.normalize-space()
========================
- identify element based visible text
- ignore white space 

Syntax:
===========
//tagname[normalize-space()='text']

3.contains():partial match
===============================
Syntax:
===========
//tagname[contains(@attribute,'partial value')]

//input[contains(@id,'searcht')]

or

//tagname[contains(text(),'partial text')]

4.starts-with():prefix value
=======================================
Syntax:
===========
//tagname[starts-with(@attribute,'partial value')]


or

//tagname[starts-with(text(),'partial text')]

//input[starts-with(@id,'twotab')]
